const pages=[
 ['Start drawing','Open Shapes and choose Rectangle, Ellipse, Triangle, Polygon, Star or Line. Drag on the canvas: the shape starts under your finger. A single tap places a standard-sized shape with its top-left corner at your finger. Pencil follows your strokes. Path lets you tap anchors and drag to curve; finish with “Finish path”.'],
 ['Select and edit','Select: tap artwork once. Drag it after a small movement threshold, or drag an empty area to select a set of shapes. Direct: tap a shape inside a group and edit its square points. Tap a point to reveal its round curve handles. Zoom in to reveal closely spaced points, or use ‹ Point / Point › to move through every point. Edit as path turns rectangles and ellipses into editable paths. Text stays editable in Properties.'],
 ['Precise movement','Objects follow your finger at the same distance. Precision reduces the movement to 35% for fine adjustments. Snap is optional and starts off. Corner and edge handles resize; the handle above rotates. Constrain keeps proportions; Resize from center uses the centre. Two fingers pan and zoom the canvas.'],
 ['Group layers','Turn on Multi-select, then tap the shapes or layer names you want. Press Group on the bottom of the canvas. Ungroup releases the shapes. Direct select edits a shape within a group. Select contents selects its children. Locked layers cannot be edited.'],
 ['Combine shapes and paths','Turn on Multi-select and choose at least two closed shapes in the same group. Unite joins their filled areas. Subtract front cuts the shapes in front out of the back shape. Keep overlap keeps only their shared area. Exclude overlap cuts away their shared area. Compound path keeps all outlines in one editable shape, with overlaps becoming holes. Combining creates editable points from the current frame and replaces the originals; Undo restores them. Join paths connects the nearest ends of two open paths.'],
 ['Animate in five steps','1. Draw or select a shape.\n2. Put the playhead at 0 seconds and press Add keyframe. This enables movement, rotation, scale and opacity tracks.\n3. Tap or drag the timeline ruler to a later time, such as 2 seconds.\n4. Move, resize or rotate the shape. Its enabled properties get new keyframes at that time.\n5. Return to the beginning and press Play. Adjust the Tween menu to choose smooth easing, linear motion or a hold.'],
 ['Animate colour or points','In Properties, tap the ◇ beside Fill or Stroke to enable colour animation, then go to a later time and change its colour. For a path, use Keyframe shape, then edit the same points later. Keep the same number of points and curve handles for a smooth shape tween. Adding/deleting points changes topology. Mesh shading is static; it follows the shape’s animated transform.'],
 ['Shade with a mesh','Select a filled shape and choose Mesh. Hold a grid point briefly to open its colour picker, or tap the point and use Point colour in the visible editing dock. Moving your finger cancels the hold so you can drag points to move the shading. A quick two-finger tap on the canvas undoes the last change; move the fingers to pinch or pan instead. More rows and More columns give you more colour points (up to 7 × 7). Subdivide cell splits the cell next to the selected point; Tap to subdivide lets you tap inside a cell to place a new row and column there. The mesh is clipped to your shape and included in video and SVG exports. This is a Poppy colour grid, with no Illustrator mesh-file import.'],
 ['Save and export','Changes save on this device. Project → Export project file makes a portable .poppy backup to open on another device. Export video renders the animation and audio together. The resolution and supported format appear before rendering. Every launch starts with a blank canvas; Project → Open local project restores saved work.'],
];
export function showHelp(a){const d=a.dialog('Help · Draw it. Tween it.',`<div class="help-intro">Your quick guide to Poppy’s Animator</div><div class="help-pages">${pages.map(([title,body],i)=>`<details ${title==='Animate in five steps'?'open':''}><summary>${title}</summary><p>${body.replaceAll('\n','<br>')}</p></details>`).join('')}</div><div class="help-shortcuts">Keyboard: V Select · A Direct select · M Mesh · R Rectangle · E Ellipse · B Path · Space Play · Ctrl/⌘Z Undo</div>`);d.classList.add('help-dialog');}
